{"agent":"sw-remoteauth","data":{"budget":"15 min, greps only","claim":"Every operator-only verb reaches identity.agent_marker or is_agent, and no caller yet feeds a paired credential into resolve_actor, so a credential bound once in services/identity and read by agent_marker, is_agent and resolve_actor applies one role check to all of them with no per-verb edit.","falsifier":"An operator-only verb that decides person-or-agent without agent_marker or is_agent.","item":"P-remote.auth","mechanism":"agent_marker is the only person-or-agent test: 18 modules ask it (approval.grant, grants.add, chore, reviewer_trust, export select, complete, claim force, config set). Today it reads only --agent, DDFLOW_AGENT and CLAUDECODE, so with no marker it answers person: that is the convention. resolve_actor takes credential_role but only the harness attest path passes one.","probe":"git grep -c -E '\\b(agent_marker|is_agent)\\(' -- 'ddflow/*.py'; git grep -n 'credential_role=' -- 'ddflow/*.py'; env -u CLAUDECODE -u DDFLOW_AGENT python3 -c \"from ddflow.services.identity import agent_marker as a; print(repr(a()))\"; git grep -n -E 'DDFLOW_TOKEN|token\\.issued' -- 'ddflow/*.py'","probe_output":"19 files carry the call (ddflow/api/chore.py:1, api/gates/_run.py:1, api/gates/_vet.py:1, api/lifecycle/claim.py:2, api/lifecycle/complete/approval.py:3, api/pin_files.py:1, api/setup/config.py:1, api/surf_setup.py:1, services/actors.py:1, services/approval.py:1, services/approvals/answer.py:1, services/approvals/relayed.py:1, services/export/select.py:1, services/gate_accept.py:1, services/grants.py:1, services/identity.py:3, services/phase_complete.py:1, services/repairs/accepted.py:1, services/reviewer_trust.py:1). credential_role=: only ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:450. agent_marker with no markers: ''. DDFLOW_TOKEN / token.issued: no hit.","question":"Can one bound credential close the operator-only gap, or does each operator verb need its own role check?","sources":[],"verdict":"